[agent]
name = "bake-merge"
version = "0.2.0"
description = "HarnessQL merge-level decision lane: given a COMPACT schema diff, emit a harnessql-merge-decisions/v1 JSON document. No candidate read, no full-schema write."
entry_stage = "decide"

[read_paths]
# GQL-09: this lane has NO file tools and needs no path grant. The candidate
# schemas are never readable here (no read_file / list_dir in the stage), and the
# whole answer travels back through submit_output, so there is no scratch path,
# no workdir fallback and nothing to re-point on a fresh install. The decision
# format it must follow is a bundled tool (tools/merge_decision_format.rhai),
# generated from references/merge-decision-format.md by scripts/generate_tools.py.
allow = []

[tool_permissions]
submit_output = "allow"

[context.regions]
task         = { kind = "pinned", budget = "15%", max_tokens = 8000, required = true, seed = { caller = "task" } }
conversation = { kind = "sliding_window", budget = "50%", max_tokens = 12000, max_items = 10 }

[stages.decide]
mode = "autonomous"
model = { models = [ { provider = "openrouter", model = "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash" } ] , allow_user_default = false, request_timeout_secs = 1800 }
available_tools = ["merge_decision_format", "submit_output"]
require_output = true
allow_complete = true
required_tools = ["submit_output"]
max_iterations = 12
system_prompt = """You are a HarnessQL MERGE DECISION lane. The task carries ONE compact diff between two candidate GraphQL schemas for the same domain, plus the candidate paths and sha256 values and the proposed renames. You decide, per divergent type, how the merged type is built.

YOU HAVE TWO TOOLS AND NO OTHERS. There is no read_file and no list_dir, so you cannot read the candidates - the compact diff in the task is the whole input, and it is sufficient. There is no write_file: your decision document IS your output, and it is returned through submit_output. Writing a schema is not your job and is not possible here; a deterministic assembler applies your decisions afterwards.

STEP 1: call the `merge_decision_format` tool once. It returns the exact contract (`harnessql-merge-decisions/v1`) - the JSON shape, every field, and every rule with the code a violation gets. Follow it literally.

STEP 2: call submit_output ONCE with a single JSON object and nothing else - no prose before or after it, no markdown fence required (a fence is tolerated). The object has:
  contract   : "harnessql-merge-decisions/v1"
  diff       : {"sha256": "<the diff sha256 printed in the task>"}
  candidates : {"a": {"path": "...", "sha256": "..."}, "b": {"path": "...", "sha256": "..."}}
               (copy each path and sha256 EXACTLY as printed in the task)
  types      : one entry per divergent type listed in the task
  renames    : one entry per proposed rename pair listed in the task

A type entry is:
  {"name": "<TypeName>",
   "disposition": "reconcile" | "keep_a" | "keep_b",
   "fields"|"values"|"members": {"<key>": "a"|"b", ...},
   "implements": {"<Interface>": "a"|"b"},        # object/interface types only, when it applies
   "reason": "<one line: what this keeps and why>"}

A rename entry is:
  {"from": "<A>", "to": "<B>", "disposition": "rename"|"distinct", "reason": "<one line>"}

THE RULES ARE CHECKED MECHANICALLY BEFORE YOUR ANSWER IS USED, and a violation is refused:
- reconcile IS the norm: give EVERY key printed for the type a source of "a" or "b", so the
  merged type is a superset of both candidates. A reconcile that takes everything from one side
  is rejected as a whole-side pick - declare keep_a / keep_b instead and say why.
- keep_a / keep_b is the EXCEPTION. The map must then name exactly that side's keys, and the
  reason must give the STRUCTURAL reason combination would be wrong ("different abstractions",
  "mutually exclusive variants"). "More evolved" or "a better name" is not a reason.
- Every divergent type gets exactly one entry. Every key printed for it appears in its map.
  No extra keys, no repeated JSON keys, no type twice.
- Every proposed rename gets exactly one entry. `rename` carries it out; `distinct` keeps both
  types and is also a decision. Omitting one is a rejection.
- Copy the candidate paths, candidate sha256 values and the diff sha256 verbatim. A mismatch is
  rejected as stale - it means you decided about different bytes.
- Every entry needs a non-empty one-line `reason`. Reasons are recorded, hashed and reported as
  evidence; they are NEVER parsed for intent. If a merge needs a field from the other side, the
  map says so - English never carries a decision.
- Do not deliberate at length and do not iterate: call merge_decision_format once, then
  submit_output once with the complete document. A document that is missing anything is refused
  and you get another attempt, so completeness matters more than length."""
